On Sat, 02 Feb 2008 12:17:03 -0800, nick.gorski wrote:

(snipping a lot of info on the character) 
> Question #1: I'm having serious issues with item identification. Up
> until the last ~2000 turns I had only found 2 scrolls of identification,
> and after blessing each only identified a few items. I burned 35 charges
> of a MM writing identify scrolls and blessing them, and none of them
> identified all. Is it worthwhile to burn more charges on a MM, and
> possibly use an already identified scroll of charging to charge it back
> up,

It may well be worth it.  Bless the scroll of charging before using it.  
You didn't ask, but: I wouldn't write a scroll of genocide unless I 
really needed it.    

Have you come across a scroll of gold detection yet?  

> 
> Question #2: Will a wand of cancellation take care of liches' magical
> attacks? I've got a 0:7 wand of cancellation, and maybe this is better
> than worrying about genocide as above.

I'm not 100% sure since I've yet to zap a lich with a /oC, but I'm fairly 
sure it will cancel their magic.  I know it works on Disenchanters but 
I'm not sure if Liches have any resistance to it. 


> 
> Question #3: I only recently discovered the joys of #twoweapon. Right
> now, I'm wielding Excalibur and a +0 silver saber, but I don't know if
> it would be better to wield a +1 dagger instead of the silver saber (I'm
> expert in dagger, and maxed out at basic in saber).  Or, if I make it
> through the castle I could wish for a shield and just wield Excalibur.
> So the question is, should I continue with #twoweapon, or switch to a
> weapon & shield?  If I do #twoweapon, should I use the saber or a dagger
> as my backup?  Am I right to assume that the silver saber will be better
> down below the castle, even though I can only advance it to basic and
> not expert as with the dagger?

I recently ascended a Valkyrie using Excalibur and a Silver Saber.  It 
does wonders later on.  A previous Valk ascension carried Excalibur/
Shield of Reflection.  Both are viable, but #twoweapon Silver Saber 
through Gehennom. When I passed through I was able to defeat almost 
everything I came across in just a few turns that way.


> Question #4: What should my wishing priorities be if I make it through
> the castle?  My plan is:
> 1. reflection -- either amulet or shield, depending on answers to above
> 2. amulet of life saving, if I go with the shield (figure it's a good
> idea for someone that's never gotten a character this far) 3. speed
> boots
> 4. gauntlets of power
> ???

1,2, and 3, I would wish for, personally.  I've also made a habit of 
wishing for Gauntlets of Power, but apparently the general opinion is 
that they're not necessary.  

Make sure you have a blessed scroll of charging before using any wishes, 
or the ability to make them.  


> 
> Useful things that I can think of -- a cloak of displacement, a weapon
